Keep the packaged sysconfig knobs, and do not pull in containerd.service.

docker.service is otherwise contrib/init/systemd/docker.service.
/etc/sysconfig/docker* is how this package passes OPTIONS,
DOCKER_STORAGE_OPTIONS, DOCKER_NETWORK_OPTIONS and INSECURE_REGISTRY.
The default listener stays -H fd:// from docker.socket.

dockerd supervises a private containerd unless OPTIONS or daemon.json
names a socket. Wants=containerd.service and --containerd= would start
the system daemon and, on a fresh data root, attach to it.

docker-network-cleanup removes network-scripts ifcfg files for veth and
docker interfaces. Those files come back as real interfaces after reboot.

--- a/contrib/init/systemd/docker.service
+++ b/contrib/init/systemd/docker.service
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 Description=Docker Application Container Engine
 Documentation=https://docs.docker.com
 After=network-online.target nss-lookup.target docker.socket firewalld.service containerd.service time-set.target
-Wants=network-online.target containerd.service
+Wants=network-online.target
 Requires=docker.socket
 StartLimitBurst=3
 StartLimitIntervalSec=60
@@ -12,7 +12,18 @@
 # the default is not to use systemd for cgroups because the delegate issues still
 # exists and systemd currently does not support the cgroup feature set required
 # for containers run by docker
-ExecStart=/usr/bin/dockerd -H fd:// --containerd=/run/containerd/containerd.sock
+EnvironmentFile=-/etc/sysconfig/docker
+EnvironmentFile=-/etc/sysconfig/docker-storage
+EnvironmentFile=-/etc/sysconfig/docker-network
+# No --containerd here: dockerd supervises a private containerd. Point
+# OPTIONS at /run/containerd/containerd.sock to use containerd.service.
+ExecStart=/usr/bin/dockerd -H fd:// \
+          $OPTIONS \
+          $DOCKER_STORAGE_OPTIONS \
+          $DOCKER_NETWORK_OPTIONS \
+          $INSECURE_REGISTRY
+ExecStartPre=/usr/bin/docker-network-cleanup
+ExecStopPost=/usr/bin/docker-network-cleanup
 ExecReload=/bin/kill -s HUP $MAINPID
 TimeoutStartSec=0
 RestartSec=2
